  "body": "On main since PR #990 merged (2026-11-12, as part of PR #1058's stack). Found by our high-tier review of PR #990 (review comment of 2026-11-12 on that PR, head ed514853); the PR merged at that same head, so the finding is in main.\n\n**What is wrong.** PR #990 makes turning sections post constant surface speed (`G50 S<clamp>`, `G96 S<m/min> M03`). The live-tool branch of `startPreamble` in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` (it writes `G98`, the C-axis-on code and the live spindle-on with its S word) never states `G97`. So a live-tool (driven tool, C-axis) section that follows a G96 turning section on a mill-turn is posted while G96 is still modal. Hand-built stream from the review, a CSS turning section then a `LiveTool` section at 3000 rpm:\n\n```\nG50 S6000\nG96 S200 M03\n...\nM05\n(T0202 EM)\nT0202\nG98\nM1001\nM1003 S3000\n```\n\nWith G96 modal, a control can read `S3000` as a surface speed (3000 m/min), not the live spindle's 3000 rpm.\n\n**Why P0.** Wrong posted G-code: the spindle speed word of a real program can mean something else on the machine. Before #990 nothing put a surface speed on the stream, so this was unreachable; now a turning op followed by a cross-drill or C-axis milling op on the same mill-turn reaches it.\n\n**Fix (from the review).** State `G97` before the live spindle-on, or in the section end after any section that posted a G96 - so no section ever starts under a spindle mode it did not state. Check `tormach-lathe.cps` (it writes `G96 D<cap>`) for the same hole, and every other section kind that can follow a G96 section (drilling on centre, threading, tapping, probing, a tool change with no spindle).\n\nDone means: the stream above posts a `G97` before `M1003 S3000`; pinned by a twin of `a_section_without_surface_speed_posts_g97_after_one_with_it` that uses a `LiveTool` section, on both lathe posts where they have a live branch; a recorded case in the per-post script suites (`crates/post/tests/recorded/`); every existing lathe golden unchanged except where it gains the `G97`.\n",
